course: dictionary
lesson: 6953
title: Long words built from parts
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Long words can look scary, but the clues around them often explain what they mean. «Scientists who study fossils are called palaeontologists.» So a palaeontologist is a scientist, and the job is to study fossils.
explain: Look at the sentences around the word. «Palaeontologists dig slowly, map where each bone lies, and wrap big bones in plaster jackets, like a cast on a broken arm, to carry them safely.» The clues are dig, bones and carry them safely: this is careful work done in the ground.
explain: Test your guess by swapping in the meaning. «Trust experts about their own subject: a doctor knows bodies, while palaeontologists, who study fossils, know about dinosaurs.» A doctor is an expert on bodies, so a palaeontologist is the expert on fossils and dinosaurs. The meaning fits every time.
fact: A palaeontologist is a scientist who studies fossils.
fact: Palaeontologists study fossils to learn about plants and animals that lived long ago, like dinosaurs.
fact: In their work, palaeontologists dig up fossils, clean them, and work out how old they are and how the creatures lived.
fact: «Palaeontologists dig slowly» because a careless hit can destroy a find that waited millions of years.
fact: In US spelling, the word is written paleontologist, but the meaning is the same.
exercise: What does a palaeontologist study? | Old coins from castles | Teeth from people who are alive today | *Fossils, to learn about plants and animals that lived long ago | Stars and planets in the night sky
exercise: «Palaeontologists dig slowly, map where each bone lies.» Why do they dig so slowly? | Because they are tired and want a rest | *To keep fossils safe from damage | To hide the bones from other scientists | To finish the dig as fast as they can
exercise: Find the word that names the same kind of expert as «palaeontologists, who study fossils». | doctor | *palaeontologist | dinosaurs | bodies
test: In plain English, what is a palaeontologist? | A doctor who looks after people who are ill | A person who sells old bones in a shop | A kind of dinosaur that lived long ago | *A scientist who studies fossils to learn about creatures that lived long ago
test: Why do palaeontologists wrap big bones in plaster jackets? | To make the bones shine brightly | To hide them from other scientists | *To carry them safely, like a cast on a broken arm | To make the bones lighter and float
exam: Mia says a palaeontologist is a kind of dinosaur. Who is right? | No, a palaeontologist is a scientist who studies fossils | Mia is right, because it is a type of plaster | *Mia is wrong, because a palaeontologist is a scientist who studies fossils | Mia is right, because it is an animal from long ago
